---
/**
 * ChemoreflexAltitude — "Altitude and the alveolar oxygen your breathing buys". The same
 * feedback loop at lower barometric pressure: the simplified alveolar gas equation,
 * alveolar PO2 = 0.21 x (PB - 47) - PaCO2 / R, with sliders for barometric pressure and
 * arterial PCO2, a toggle for R, and an optional shaded band of about 50 to 60 mmHg of
 * alveolar PO2 (Weil and colleagues' isocapnic subjects). A stacked bar splits the humidified
 * inspired PO2 into the alveolar PO2 and the carbon dioxide term. Self-contained
 * vanilla-TS Astro island. Original.
 */
---

<figure class="cb card" data-chemoalt>
  <figcaption class="cha-head">Altitude and the alveolar oxygen your breathing buys<span class="cha-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <svg class="cha-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 214" role="img" aria-label="A bar chart of partial pressures in millimetres of mercury. The top bar is the humidified inspired oxygen partial pressure. The second bar splits that same length into the calculated alveolar oxygen partial pressure and the carbon dioxide term, arterial PCO2 divided by the respiratory exchange ratio. A dashed line marks the alveolar value if arterial PCO2 were 40 millimetres of mercury. An optional shaded band marks alveolar PO2 of about 50 to 60 millimetres of mercury.">
    <rect data-band x="111.5" y="72" width="19.5" height="32" fill="#e57200" fill-opacity="0.2" stroke="#e57200" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 2" style="display:none"></rect>

    <text x="14" y="30" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="a">Humidified inspired PO₂ = 95.1 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="35" width="10" height="14" fill="#c9d3dd" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-a></rect>

    <text x="14" y="70" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="b">Alveolar PO₂ (calculated) = 45.1 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="75" width="10" height="14" fill="#0e7c86" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-alv></rect>
    <rect x="24" y="75" width="10" height="14" fill="#e57200" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-co2></rect>
    <line x1="14" y1="72" x2="14" y2="93" stroke="#1f1f27" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 2" data-ref></line>

    <line x1="14" y1="104" x2="326" y2="104" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1"></line>
    <g data-ticks></g>
    <text x="170" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55">partial pressure (mmHg)</text>

    <rect x="14" y="144" width="10" height="10" fill="#0e7c86" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="0.8"></rect>
    <text x="30" y="153" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="l1">alveolar PO₂ = 95.13 − 50.00 = 45.13 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="158" width="10" height="10" fill="#e57200" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="0.8"></rect>
    <text x="30" y="167" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="l2">CO₂ term = PaCO₂ ÷ R = 40 ÷ 0.80 = 50.0 mmHg</text>
    <line x1="14" y1="178" x2="24" y2="178" stroke="#1f1f27" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 2"></line>
    <text x="30" y="181" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="l3">dashed line: alveolar PO₂ if PaCO₂ were 40 mmHg = 45.1 mmHg</text>
    <g data-band-key style="display:none">
      <rect x="14" y="186" width="10" height="10" fill="#e57200" fill-opacity="0.2" stroke="#e57200" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 2"></rect>
      <text x="30" y="195" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55">shaded: about 50 to 60 mmHg, where Weil and colleagues’</text>
      <text x="30" y="207" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55">isocapnic subjects’ response steepened; not a threshold</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <div class="cha-controls">
    <label class="cha-slabel"><span>Barometric pressure PB <em data-out="pb">500</em> mmHg <small>(760 is the lesson’s sea-level anchor)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="pb" min="400" max="760" step="10" value="500" />
    </label>
    <label class="cha-slabel"><span>Arterial PCO₂ (PaCO₂) <em data-out="pco2">40</em> mmHg <small>(about 40 in an adult at rest at sea level)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="pco2" min="20" max="50" step="1" value="40" />
    </label>
    <fieldset class="cha-fs">
      <legend>Respiratory exchange ratio R</legend>
      <label class="cha-opt"><input type="radio" data-r-opt value="0.8" checked /> 0.80 <small>(the lesson’s value)</small></label>
      <label class="cha-opt"><input type="radio" data-r-opt value="1" /> 1.00 <small>(hypothetical, not the lesson’s value)</small></label>
    </fieldset>
    <label class="cha-opt cha-band-opt"><input type="checkbox" data-band-toggle /> Shade the alveolar PO₂ band of about 50 to 60 mmHg</label>
  </div>

  <dl class="cha-readout">
    <div><dt>Humidified inspired PO₂, 0.21 × (PB − 47)</dt><dd><span data-r="pio2">95.1</span> mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>CO₂ term, PaCO₂ ÷ R</dt><dd><span data-r="term">50.0</span> mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Alveolar PO₂ (calculated)</dt><dd><span data-r="pao2">45.1</span> mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>CO₂ washout gain, (40 − PaCO₂) ÷ R</dt><dd><span data-r="gain">0.0</span> mmHg</dd></div>
    <div class="cha-wide"><dt>Calculated alveolar PO₂ against the isocapnic band of about 50 to 60 mmHg (one group of subjects; not a threshold; resting PCO₂ only)</dt><dd data-r="pos">below the band</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <p class="cha-why" data-why role="status"></p>

  <p class="cha-assume"><strong>In this sketch:</strong> steady state, a person breathing air, inspired oxygen fraction fixed at 0.21, water vapour pressure fixed at 47 mmHg and negligible inspired carbon dioxide; these are the lesson’s stipulated model values for its worked problem, not measurements from any named mountain. R = 0.80 is the lesson’s value; R = 1.00 is hypothetical, not the lesson’s value, and is invented for this sketch. The slider ranges are made up (760 mmHg is the lesson’s sea-level anchor), and the sketch does not say which combinations a person reaches. The reference PaCO₂ of 40 mmHg is the lesson’s value for an adult at rest at sea level. The band of about 50 to 60 mmHg comes from one group of normal human subjects, Weil and colleagues’, studied under isocapnia (alveolar PCO₂ held at its resting value); it is not a threshold. The values shown are alveolar, not arterial, PO₂. The sketch sets PCO₂ by hand and does not predict how much a person hyperventilates.</p>

  <p class="cha-foot">Alveolar PO₂ = 0.21 × (PB − 47) − PaCO₂ ÷ R. A lower barometric pressure lowers the first term; washing out carbon dioxide raises the result by (40 − PaCO₂) ÷ R. The rule gives alveolar PO₂, not arterial PO₂.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const INK = '#4b4b55';
  const FIO2 = 0.21;       // lesson's worked problem
  const PH2O = 47;         // mmHg, saturated water vapour (lesson)
  const PCO2_REF = 40;     // mmHg, lesson's arterial PCO2 before hyperventilation
  const BAND_LO = 50, BAND_HI = 60; // mmHg, Weil and colleagues' isocapnic subjects
  const AX_MAX = 160;
  const X0 = 14, X1 = 326;
  const xs = (v: number) => X0 + (Math.max(0, Math.min(AX_MAX, v)) / AX_MAX) * (X1 - X0);
  const MINUS = '−';
  let uid = 0;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-chemoalt]').forEach((root) => {
    uid += 1;
    const inp = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="' + k + '"]');
    const out = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="' + k + '"]');
    const rd = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-r="' + k + '"]');
    const tx = (k: string) => root.querySelector<SVGTextElement>('[data-t="' + k + '"]');
    const rect = (k: string) => root.querySelector<SVGRectElement>('[' + k + ']');
    const pbIn = inp('pb'), coIn = inp('pco2');
    const pbOut = out('pb'), coOut = out('pco2');
    const rPio2 = rd('pio2'), rTerm = rd('term'), rPao2 = rd('pao2'), rGain = rd('gain'), rPos = rd('pos');
    const tA = tx('a'), tB = tx('b'), tL1 = tx('l1'), tL2 = tx('l2'), tL3 = tx('l3');
    const barA = rect('data-bar-a'), barAlv = rect('data-bar-alv'), barCo2 = rect('data-bar-co2');
    const refLine = root.querySelector<SVGLineElement>('[data-ref]');
    const bandG = root.querySelector<SVGRectElement>('[data-band]');
    const bandKey = root.querySelector<SVGGElement>('[data-band-key]');
    const bandToggle = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-band-toggle]');
    const why = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-why]');
    const ticks = root.querySelector<SVGGElement>('[data-ticks]');
    const rOpts = Array.from(root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-r-opt]'));
    if (!pbIn || !coIn || !pbOut || !coOut || !rPio2 || !rTerm || !rPao2 || !rGain || !rPos ||
        !tA || !tB || !tL1 || !tL2 || !tL3 || !barA || !barAlv || !barCo2 || !refLine || !bandG || !bandKey ||
        !bandToggle || !why || !ticks || rOpts.length !== 2) return;

    rOpts.forEach((o) => o.setAttribute('name', 'cha-r-' + uid));

    // axis ticks every 20 mmHg
    for (let v = 0; v <= AX_MAX; v += 20) {
      const x = xs(v);
      const ln = document.createElementNS(NS, 'line');
      ln.setAttribute('x1', String(x)); ln.setAttribute('x2', String(x));
      ln.setAttribute('y1', '104'); ln.setAttribute('y2', '108');
      ln.setAttribute('stroke', INK); ln.setAttribute('stroke-width', '1');
      ticks.appendChild(ln);
      const t = document.createElementNS(NS, 'text');
      t.setAttribute('x', String(x)); t.setAttribute('y', '119');
      t.setAttribute('text-anchor', v === 0 ? 'start' : v === AX_MAX ? 'end' : 'middle');
      t.setAttribute('font-size', '9'); t.setAttribute('fill', INK);
      t.textContent = String(v);
      ticks.appendChild(t);
    }

    const f1 = (n: number) => n.toFixed(1);
    const f2 = (n: number) => n.toFixed(2);
    const sgn = (n: number) => (n < -0.05 ? MINUS + Math.abs(n).toFixed(1) : n > 0.05 ? '+' + n.toFixed(1) : '0.0');
    const getR = () => {
      const sel = rOpts.find((o) => o.checked);
      return sel && sel.value === '1' ? 1 : 0.8;
    };
    const rTxt = (r: number) => r.toFixed(2);

    function render() {
      const pb = parseInt(pbIn!.value, 10);
      const pco2 = parseInt(coIn!.value, 10);
      const r = getR();
      const pio2 = FIO2 * (pb - PH2O);
      const term = pco2 / r;
      const pao2 = pio2 - term;
      const refPao2 = pio2 - PCO2_REF / r;
      const gain = (PCO2_REF - pco2) / r;
      const pao2r = Math.round(pao2 * 10) / 10; // classify on the displayed value
      const pos: 'above' | 'inside' | 'below' = pao2r > BAND_HI ? 'above' : pao2r >= BAND_LO ? 'inside' : 'below';
      const bandOn = bandToggle!.checked;

      pbOut!.textContent = String(pb);
      coOut!.textContent = String(pco2);

      rPio2!.textContent = f1(pio2);
      rTerm!.textContent = f1(term);
      rPao2!.textContent = f1(pao2);
      rGain!.textContent = sgn(gain);
      rPos!.textContent = pos === 'above' ? 'above the band' : pos === 'inside' ? 'inside the band' : 'below the band';

      // SVG
      tA!.textContent = 'Humidified inspired PO₂ = ' + f1(pio2) + ' mmHg';
      tB!.textContent = 'Alveolar PO₂ (calculated) = ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg';
      tL1!.textContent = 'alveolar PO₂ = ' + f2(pio2) + ' − ' + f2(term) + ' = ' + f2(pao2) + ' mmHg';
      tL2!.textContent = 'CO₂ term = PaCO₂ ÷ R = ' + pco2 + ' ÷ ' + rTxt(r) + ' = ' + f1(term) + ' mmHg';
      tL3!.textContent = 'dashed line: alveolar PO₂ if PaCO₂ were 40 mmHg = ' + f1(refPao2) + ' mmHg';
      const wA = xs(pio2) - X0;
      const wAlv = xs(pao2) - X0;
      barA!.setAttribute('width', wA.toFixed(1));
      barAlv!.setAttribute('width', Math.max(0, wAlv).toFixed(1));
      barCo2!.setAttribute('x', (X0 + Math.max(0, wAlv)).toFixed(1));
      barCo2!.setAttribute('width', Math.max(0, wA - Math.max(0, wAlv)).toFixed(1));
      const xr = xs(refPao2);
      refLine!.setAttribute('x1', xr.toFixed(1));
      refLine!.setAttribute('x2', xr.toFixed(1));
      bandG!.style.display = bandOn ? '' : 'none';
      bandKey!.style.display = bandOn ? '' : 'none';

      // status
      let s = 'In this sketch, at a barometric pressure of ' + pb + ' mmHg the humidified inspired PO₂ is ' + f1(pio2) +
        ' mmHg, and with arterial PCO₂ at ' + pco2 + ' mmHg and R = ' + rTxt(r) + ' the calculated alveolar PO₂ is ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg.';
      if (pco2 < PCO2_REF) {
        s += ' In this sketch, setting arterial PCO₂ to ' + pco2 + ' mmHg instead of 40 gives (40 ' + MINUS + ' ' + pco2 + ') ÷ ' + rTxt(r) + ' = ' + f1(gain) +
          ' mmHg more calculated alveolar PO₂ than at 40 mmHg.';
      } else if (pco2 === PCO2_REF) {
        s += ' In this sketch, an arterial PCO₂ of 40 mmHg gives no washout gain; lowering PCO₂ with the slider raises the calculated alveolar PO₂.';
      } else {
        s += ' In this sketch, an arterial PCO₂ of ' + pco2 + ' mmHg, above 40, gives ' + f1(-gain) + ' mmHg less calculated alveolar PO₂ than at 40 mmHg: the rule run in the other direction.';
      }
      if (r === 1) {
        s += ' R = 1.00 is hypothetical, not the lesson’s value (0.80); a larger R makes the CO₂ term, and so the washout gain, smaller.';
      }
      if (pb === 760 && pco2 === 40 && r === 0.8) {
        s += ' This is the lesson’s sea-level anchor, 99.7 mmHg, close to the alveolar PO₂ of about 100 mmHg usually quoted for an adult at rest at sea level.';
      } else if (pb === 500 && r === 0.8 && (pco2 === 40 || pco2 === 30)) {
        s += ' This matches the lesson’s worked problem at 500 mmHg (45.1 mmHg at PaCO₂ 40, 57.6 mmHg at 30), which is a model result rather than a measured acclimatization benefit.';
      }
      if (bandOn) {
        if (pos === 'above') {
          s += ' In this sketch, the calculated alveolar PO₂ is above the shaded band of about 50 to 60 mmHg; the lesson describes the response to alveolar PO₂ as shallow above about 60 mmHg in Weil and colleagues’ subjects, studied under isocapnia.';
        } else if (pos === 'inside') {
          s += ' In this sketch, the calculated alveolar PO₂ is inside the shaded band of about 50 to 60 mmHg, where the response to alveolar PO₂ steepened in Weil and colleagues’ normal subjects, studied under isocapnia.';
        } else {
          s += ' In this sketch, the calculated alveolar PO₂ is below the shaded band of about 50 to 60 mmHg; the lesson does not describe the response curve at values that low.';
        }
        s += ' The band is from one group of subjects and is not a threshold.';
        if (pco2 !== PCO2_REF) {
          s += ' Here arterial PCO₂ is not the lesson’s resting 40 mmHg, and the lesson says the curve’s shape depends on the prevailing PCO₂, so the band should not be read across to this state.';
        }
      }
      if (pco2 < PCO2_REF) {
        s += ' This sketch sets PCO₂ by hand and does not predict how much a person hyperventilates; the lesson notes that the alkalosis restrains hyperventilation until the kidney acts.';
      }
      why!.textContent = s;
    }

    [pbIn, coIn, bandToggle, ...rOpts].forEach((el) => {
      el.addEventListener('input', render);
      el.addEventListener('change', render);
    });
    render();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .cb { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .cha-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .cha-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .cha-svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; height: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .cha-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .cha-slabel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .cha-slabel small, .cha-opt small { font-size: inherit; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .cha-slabel em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-accent); font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .cha-slabel input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .cha-fs { margin: 0; padding: 0; border: 0; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .cha-fs legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: 0.15rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .cha-opt { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .cha-opt input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .cha-band-opt { align-self: end; }
  .cha-readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2); margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0; padding: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-3); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ddp-color-accent) 8%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; }
  .cha-readout div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; }
  .cha-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .cha-readout dt { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .cha-readout dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .cha-why { margin: 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; min-height: 9em; }
  .cha-assume { margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); line-height: 1.45; }
  .cha-foot { margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-secondary); padding-left: 0.55rem; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .cha-controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cha-readout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .cha-why { min-height: 14em; }
  }
</style>
